                <pb facs="0307" n="195" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg195"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/3577: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-03"><hi rendition="#italic">January 3,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received January 4, 12:49 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following from [Harris at] Omsk.</p>
                <p>“6. 3rd. Ufa has been evacuated by Siberian troops and small detachment Allied
                    troops stationed there. While it is claimed that relinquishing Ufa has no great
                    military signification, yet the moral effect on general situation is not good.
                    Harris.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
